From d1db6821fd51bc23ae6c5d63a012e9fa4a259396 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Liam Curtis <liamcurtis81@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 16:43:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 26/27] ASP: Midway speed-ups (idle skip, sound ROM mapping,
 timer division)

- TMS34010 idle skipping for Mortal Kombat and MK II: the wait-for-vblank
  loop (list walk + flag poll) was over half the CPU's time. When the flag
  is zero, from that loop, and the lists are empty, the rest of the slice up
  to the CPU timer is counted as spent. Pictures and sound identical to
  before for 1500 frames; after that the attract demo picks different
  fighters, as the timing feeds the game's randomness.
- MK/NBA Jam sound ROM mapped directly instead of through the read handler.
- BurnTimer's 64-bit divisions (software routines on this CPU) replaced by
  an exact VFP-estimated quotient with integer correction.
Also: profiling hooks under ASP_PCPROF (not in normal builds).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JCu91LrG764XV67j6TkDrQ
